      "id": "TE-C59-wind",
      "sequence": 1780,
      "title": "గాలి (gāli) — wind, air",
      "headword": "గాలి",
      "romanization": "gāli",
      "gloss": "wind, air",
      "script": "telugu",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:616b2faabc1494f5",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: what did antē mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: గాలి",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "గాలి (gāli) — \"wind, air\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "గాలి (gāli) is inherited, and it covers both the wind that blows and the air that is simply there. Telugu does not split them."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It reaches further than weather. గాలి (gāli) is breath, and it is rumour — గాలి (gāli) వార్త is a story with nothing holding it up, blown in from somewhere. Air, breath and hearsay under one word is a chain a great many languages make, and it usually starts with breathing."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A గాలి (gāli) getting up in the evening is the ordinary reason given for cutting a visit short."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first reason to start saying goodbye."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "gāli",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *gāli*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "gāli, then veḷḷostānu, and use the one as a reason for the other",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *gāli*, then *veḷḷostānu*, and use the one as a reason for the other]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does గాలి (gāli) mean? (\"wind, air\".) Say it once more."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
