        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ఇసుక",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఇసుక (isuka) — \"sand\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఇసుక (isuka) is inherited and unremarkable, and that is the point: it is the ground beside every నది in the Telugu country."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The sand of a riverbed is where cattle are watered, where lorries come at night to dig, and where a village argument about who owns the river tends to start. A plain word can carry a lot of local weather."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఇసుకలో నీళ్ళు, water in sand, is what you say about effort that soaks away."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
