        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: బురద",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "బురద (burada) — \"mud\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "బురద (burada) is mud — what ఇసుక (isuka) becomes when the rain has been at it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It does the same second job that mud does in English. బురద (burada) చల్లు, to throw mud, is to slander somebody, and the picture is exact enough that you can guess the phrase before you are told it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "బురద (burada) is also the honest reason a visit ends early in the wet months. The బాట between the గ్రామం and the నది turns to it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
